---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const title = "Privacy Policy – PotionPals";
---

<Layout title={title} lang="en" favicon="apps/potionpals/favicon.png" description="Privacy Policy – PotionPals." robots="noindex, follow">
    <main>
        <section>
            <nav aria-label="PotionPals documents"><a href="/apps/potionpals/">PotionPals</a> · <a href="/apps/potionpals/terms-of-use/">Terms of Use</a> · <a href="/pt-br/apps/potionpals/privacy-policy/" lang="pt-BR">Português</a></nav>
            <h1>{title}</h1>
            <p class="updated">Last updated: October 17, 2026</p>

            <h2>1. Scope and contact</h2>
            <p>This policy covers the PotionPals: Water Sort game for iPhone, including the test versions distributed through TestFlight, provided by Adriano Souza Costa. Send privacy questions or requests to <a href="mailto:adrianosouzacostaios@gmail.com">adrianosouzacostaios@gmail.com</a>. Website privacy preferences are separate from the app.</p>

            <h2>2. No account and no personal data</h2>
            <p>PotionPals does not require registration and does not ask for your name, email, phone number, photos, contacts or precise location. Ads appear only as optional rewarded videos, described in section 8.</p>

            <h2>3. Progress on your device and iCloud backup</h2>
            <p>Your progress, levels, stars, chapters, stories seen, challenges, high scores, coins, energy, boosters, settings and the game in progress are stored on your iPhone so you can continue where you left off. When iCloud is on, the game also keeps a copy of that progress in your iCloud account automatically, through Apple’s key-value storage. That backup stays under the control of Apple and your Apple Account, under Apple’s <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Privacy Policy</a>, and the developer has no access to it. You can bring it back with <em>Restore iCloud backup</em> in the game settings, and erase your progress with <em>Erase history and rankings</em>.</p>

            <h2>4. Game Center</h2>
            <p>Game Center is optional. If you are signed in, Apple handles your player identity, leaderboard scores and achievements under its own terms and <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Privacy Policy</a>. If you are not signed in, the game keeps working normally without it.</p>

            <h2>5. Notifications</h2>
            <p>The app may ask, once, for permission to notify you when your energy is full. These are local notifications scheduled on your device. You can change this permission at any time in iOS Settings.</p>

            <h2>6. In-app purchases</h2>
            <p>Coins, boosters and Infinite Energy are sold through the App Store. Apple processes payments, and the developer does not receive your card details. To validate purchases, deliver items and restore Infinite Energy, the app uses RevenueCat, which receives an anonymous app user identifier, transaction details and basic technical information such as device model, system and app version, region and IP address. RevenueCat handles this data under its <a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Privacy Policy</a>, and the data is used only to operate purchases. In TestFlight versions, purchases use Apple’s test environment and are not charged.</p>

            <h2>7. Usage statistics</h2>
            <p>To understand how the game is played and to improve it, the app sends usage statistics to Himetrica, an analytics service. The data is linked to the same anonymous identifier used for purchases, never to your name or email, and includes:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>screens opened and game events, such as levels started, won or lost, modes played, chapters unlocked and rewards claimed;</li>
                <li>offers shown and purchases made, with the product and where it was offered, without payment details;</li>
                <li>a profile summary in ranges, such as current chapter, stars, coins, number of purchases and streaks;</li>
                <li>the state of permissions and settings, such as notifications, Game Center, sound, music, haptics, color-blind mode and language;</li>
                <li>the app version, the install channel (App Store or TestFlight) and basic technical information about the device.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Himetrica uses the IP address to estimate an approximate location (country, region or city) and, according to <a href="https://himetrica.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">its policy</a>, does not keep the IP address in its analytics database. This data is not used for advertising or to track you in other apps. If you turn off the option that lets apps ask to track, in iOS Settings &gt; Privacy &amp; Security &gt; Tracking, the app stops sending these statistics.</p>

            <h2>8. Sharing and advertising</h2>
            <p>We do not sell or rent your data. Data is handled only by the services described in this policy, for the purposes stated.</p>
            <p>The game offers optional rewarded videos: you choose to watch one to get one more energy, a hint or an undo. These videos are served by Google AdMob, which may collect device identifiers (including the advertising identifier, IDFA, only if you allow tracking), IP address, approximate location and ad interaction data to show, measure and limit ads and to prevent fraud, under <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google’s advertising policies</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Privacy Policy</a>. Before the first video, the app shows Google’s consent message where the law requires one (for example in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, Switzerland and some US states) and asks for the iOS tracking permission. If you do not allow tracking, ads are still shown, but they are not personalized with the IDFA. Where required, you can review your ad choices again in the game’s Settings, under “Ad privacy”.</p>
            <p>To confirm that a video was watched before giving the reward, RevenueCat receives the ad event (ad network, placement, reward and revenue of that impression) linked to the same anonymous identifier used for purchases. If you deny tracking, Himetrica stops receiving usage statistics, as described in section 7.</p>

            <h2>9. Retention, deletion and privacy requests</h2>
            <p>Local data stays on your device until you delete the app or its data. The iCloud backup stays in your iCloud account until it is replaced or you remove it. Purchase records are kept by Apple and RevenueCat as needed to provide and restore purchases and to meet legal obligations. Usage statistics are kept for Himetrica’s retention period. Support emails are kept as long as needed to answer the request. For access, correction, deletion or other rights under applicable privacy laws, including the LGPD where applicable, write to <a href="mailto:adrianosouzacostaios@gmail.com">adrianosouzacostaios@gmail.com</a>. Because we do not collect identifying information, we may need details from you to locate a specific record.</p>

            <h2>10. Security and children</h2>
            <p>We use the security features provided by iOS and by the services above. No storage or transmission method is perfectly secure. PotionPals does not knowingly collect personal information from children. Parents or guardians who believe a child sent personal information through support can contact us so we can review and handle the request. Purchases can be controlled through Apple’s Screen Time and Ask to Buy features.</p>

            <h2>11. Changes</h2>
            <p>We will update this page and its revision date when our practices change, with any additional notice or consent required by applicable law.</p>
        </section>
    </main>
</Layout>

<style>
    main {
        padding: calc(64px + var(--safe-area-top)) var(--safe-page-padding-right) calc(64px + var(--safe-area-bottom)) var(--safe-page-padding-left);
        max-width: 780px;
        margin: 0 auto;
    }
    p {
        margin-bottom: 16px;
        color: var(--text-secondary);
    }
    ul {
        margin: 0 0 16px;
        padding-left: 24px;
        list-style: disc;
        color: var(--text-secondary);
    }
    li { margin-bottom: 8px; }
    nav { margin-bottom: 24px; color: var(--text-secondary); }
    h2 { font-size: 1.25rem; }
    a { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
    h1 { margin-bottom: 32px; }
    h2, .updated { margin-top: 32px; margin-bottom: 12px; }
    a { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
</style>
